PMID:39415279,PubMed,39415279,Effect of Sinetrol,weight,"There was a trend for decrease in visceral adipose tissue (VAT), BMI over time and body weight displayed a trend for dose dependent decrease.",,,,,,,,n = 20,detail_hint,expansion_queue,pending,,s12986-024-00851-7.pdf,1.000,9,Bifidobacterium have also shown to increase with polyphenol consumption,16 weeks,,n = 20,adiposity; microbiota; HDL; HbA1C; LDL; BMI; body weight; glucose; body fat; fat mass,"Muralidharan et al. Nutrition & Metabolism (2024) 21:83 https://doi.org/10.1186/s12986-024-00851-7 RESEARCH Effect of Sinetrol® Xpur on metabolic health and adiposity by interactions with gut microbiota: a randomized, open label, dose– response clinical trial Jananee Muralidharan1, Cindy Romain1, Linda Chung2, Pedro Alcaraz2, Francisco Javier Martínez‑Noguera2, Mayoura Keophiphath3, Benjamin Lelouvier4, Patricia Ancel5, Benedicte Gaborit5 and Julien Cases1* Abstract Background Sinetrol ® Xpur is a polyphenolic ingredient rich in citrus flavonoids that has shown weight loss effects in previous studies. The dose dependent nature, gut microbial actions of this product has not been explored previ‑ ously, thus presented in this study. Methods In this open label study, we evaluated the effect of Sinetrol® Xpur supplementation on healthy but over‑ weight/obese adults (20–50 yrs) for 16 weeks. P",bacillus and; Bifidobacterium have,,,16 weeks; 90 days,n = 20; 2 participants,randomized; open label; clinical trial; parallel; pilot; crossover; controlled trial,diet; supplement,p = 0.06; p < 0.005; p = 0.01; p = 0.04,"1800 mg/day; 900 mg/day; decrease in visceral adipose tissue (VAT), BMI over time and body weight displayed a tre; decrease; increased in HD and LD respectively were negatively associated to VAT; increased butyrate producers such as Eubacterium ruminantium and Ruminococcaceae NK4A214; decrease visceral adipose tissue via changes in gut microbiota; changes were made; increase in the global obesity epidemic have led to the development of several preventio; 10%; changes in gut microbiota is an important part of elucidating the mechanism of action; increase with polyphenol consumption [16]; changes in gut microbiota; 0.24%; 0.54%; 30 kg/m; 25%; 32%","Nutrition & Metabolism (2024) 21:83 https://doi.org/10.1186/s12986-024-00851-7 RESEARCH Effect of Sinetrol® Xpur on metabolic health and adiposity by interactions with gut microbiota: a randomized, open label, dose– response clinical trial Jananee Muralidharan1, Cindy Romain1, Linda Chung2, Pedro Alcaraz2, Francisco Javier Martínez‑Noguera2, Mayoura Keophiph || Methods In this open label study, we evaluated the effect of Sinetrol® Xpur supplementation on healthy but over‑ weight/obese adults (20–50 yrs) for 16 weeks. || Results We observed HDL, HbA1C, LDL and leptin improved significantly over 16 weeks, irrespective of the dosage. || Conclusions Overall chronic supplementation of Sinetrol® Xpur, irrespective of their dose improved HDL, HbA1c, LDL and leptin and tended to decrease visceral adipose tissue via changes in gut microbiota. || Keywords Obesity, Polyphenols, Gut microbiota, Fat loss, Metabolism Open Access © The Author(s) 2024. || Fla - vanones such as naringenin and hesperidin have shown glucose lowering and lipid modulating effects in invitro studies, however the human studies have shown incon - sistent results [10, 11].","Muralidharan et al. Nutrition & Metabolism (2024) 21:83 https://doi.org/10.1186/s12986-024-00851-7 RESEARCH Effect of Sinetrol® Xpur on metabolic health and adiposity by interactions with gut microbiota: a randomized, open label, dose– response clinical trial Jananee Muralidharan1, Cindy Romain1, Linda Chung2, Pedro Alcaraz2, Francisco Javier Martínez‑Noguera2, Mayoura Keophiphath3, Benjamin Lelouvier4, Patricia Ancel5, Benedicte Gaborit5 and Julien Cases1* Abstract Background Sinetrol ® Xpur is a polyphenolic ingredient rich in citrus flavonoids that has shown weight loss effects in previous studies. The